245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Sequential architecture is a type of neural network design in which layers are stacked sequentially, one after the other. Each layer in a Sequential model receives input from the previous layer and passes its output to the next layer. This linear stack of layers forms the backbone of the neural network, with data flowing through the layers in a single direction, from input to output.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
