/ActualText (Convolutional layer selection: In our proposed CNN model, we used Conv2D. We have used three conv2D layers in our model.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 477 0 R
/ActualText (Pooling layer selection: In this model, we have used Maxpooling2D. For every Conv2D layer, we have used a Maxpool2D layer. Therefore, we have used three Max-Pool2D layers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/ActualText (Flatten Layer: In our model, after using the pooling layer, we used a flatten layer to flatten the whole network.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 479 0 R
/ActualText (Dense Layer: After the flatten layer, we have used two dense layers. The dense layers are also known as fully connected layers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
